        "title": "Recap: Reading EDR Alerts Across Vendors",
        "body": "This module applied the triage mindset to real tool output. Start with the tool itself.\n\n### What EDR and an alert are\n**EDR (Endpoint Detection and Response)** is an agent on each host that continuously records process, file, network, and registry activity. Unlike legacy antivirus, which mostly matches known-bad file signatures, EDR watches behavior over time and keeps a rolling window of telemetry so analysts can look backward. A **detection** (CrowdStrike's word) or **alert** is the vendor's claim that telemetry matched a suspicious pattern. It is not yet a verdict: it still has to go through triage.\n\n### CrowdStrike Falcon fields\nCommandLine, ParentImageFileName, and ParentCommandLine together answer most of the 'what' and 'how'. SHA256String holds the file hash. Severity is a numeric score and SeverityName is one of Informational, Low, Medium, High, or Critical. Tactic and Technique carry ATT&CK names such as Stealth and Obfuscated Files or Information. ATT&CK v19 renamed the old Defense Evasion tactic to Stealth and moved tool and log tampering into a new Defense Impairment tactic, so older consoles and reports may still show Defense Evasion.\n\n### Microsoft Defender fields\nDefender exposes telemetry through advanced hunting tables queried with KQL. The key table for processes is DeviceProcessEvents. CrowdStrike calls the launching process the Parent; Microsoft calls it the Initiating process. SHA256 is usually not populated in this table, so rely on SHA1. InitiatingProcessParentFileName names the grandparent, one level further up the chain.",
        "keyPoints": [
          "EDR watches behavior over time, while legacy antivirus mostly matches known-bad signatures; an alert is a claim, not a verdict",
          "Falcon's Tactic and Technique fields use ATT&CK names; v19 renamed Defense Evasion to Stealth and added Defense Impairment",
          "Microsoft's 'Initiating' fields equal CrowdStrike's 'Parent' fields, and InitiatingProcessParentFileName is the grandparent"
        ]
